# <type>(<scope>): <subject>
#
# <body>
#
# <footer>
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Conventional Commits — enforced by .commitlintrc.json
# (@commitlint/config-conventional) via the commit-msg hook.
#
# type      required, lowercase, one of:
#             feat      a new user-facing capability
#             fix       a bug fix
#             docs      documentation only
#             style     formatting only, no behaviour change
#             refactor  neither fixes a bug nor adds a feature
#             perf      improves performance
#             test      adds or corrects tests
#             build     build system or dependencies
#             ci        CI configuration and workflows
#             chore     maintenance that does not touch src or tests
#             revert    reverts a previous commit
#
# scope     optional, lowercase, the area touched: (web), (ui), (infra),
#             (workflow), (deps). Omit rather than inventing one.
#
# subject   required, imperative mood ("add", not "added" or "adds"),
#             no trailing period, whole header <= 100 characters.
#
# body      optional, blank line before it. Explain WHY, not WHAT — the diff
#             already shows what changed. Wrap at 72 characters.
#
# footer    optional. Use for issue links and breaking changes:
#             Closes #123
#             BREAKING CHANGE: <what broke and what to do about it>
#           A breaking change may also be flagged with ! after the scope:
#             refactor(ui)!: drop the legacy Button variant prop
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Rules that matter beyond the format:
#
#   * Keep commits atomic — one logical concern each. Split unrelated
#     changes rather than bundling them.
#   * Never add trailers such as "Generated with Claude Code", author, or
#     co-author lines. The commit author is whoever ran git commit.
#
# See .github/COMMIT_CONVENTION.md for splitting guidance.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
